# Actor kind $97 (Kind97Start, $84:9F4F) in its other ways. Stage a5 s1
# places one kind $97 (record $0BAB) with $07 = $01, a sender, which no
# play meets from its start: the state was saved after it started.
# A. Its record put back to state $0C with $07 = $00, a dropper: after 30
# frames, once the range point (the view's x + $80) is within $0300-$08D5
# on the walk right (frame 574 here), it drops a kind $37 child from $50
# above that point (Kind97DropChild) and waits for the child's record to
# be free. A kind $37 started there stops the game: its start entry
# ($83:8CAB) is its wait routine Kind37Wait ($83:BD22), entered by the
# loop's JMP though it returns as a JSR'd routine (no level places a
# dropper, so no play meets this). So the free list's top entry ($15C8,
# then $0CEB) is made $0B0B, a record before the dropper's: the child is
# made there after the loop has passed it, and its state is cleared before
# it would start. The dropper then sees its child's record free, and goes
# back to its timer ($78 frames); the part ends before its next drop.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a5_s1.state
poke 000BB2 00
poke 000BAB 0C
hold RIGHT 300
hold RIGHT 272
poke 0015C8 0B,0B
hold RIGHT 2
poke 000B0B 00
hold RIGHT 12
# B. Put back to state $0C with $07 = $01: the sender's start. Then $07
# made $00 while it waits to send: its window is then the second one
# ($0110-$0410), and the pair goes out on the walk right.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a5_s1.state
poke 000BB2 01
poke 000BAB 0C
wait 4
poke 000BB2 00
hold RIGHT 300
# C. As placed (a sender, already started): on the walk right it sends a
# pair in its first window ($0120-$0300) and waits until it is gone.
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a5_s1.state
hold RIGHT 300
hold RIGHT 300
